From 0d3c5dc1bb56cc4908f217daaa4ab8aee9663979 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:21:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jail: do not lock SECBIT_KEEP_CAPS

With a capability set to apply, ujail locks SECBIT_KEEP_CAPS off before
the exec. prctl(PR_SET_KEEPCAPS) then fails with EPERM, so a service
that drops to its own user and keeps part of its capabilities across
setuid(), as dnsmasq does, cannot start under a capabilities file
("setting capabilities failed: Operation not permitted").

Leave the bit unlocked. It only lets a process keep capabilities it
already holds, within the bounding set, and execve() clears it. The OCI
runtime specification does not mention securebits, and runc and crun
set and clear PR_SET_KEEPCAPS themselves without locking it.

Fixes: acf36f2777ae ("jail: seteuid before clone(CLONE_NEWUSER)")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 jail/jail.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/jail/jail.c b/jail/jail.c
index 46727e9..46d9f35 100644
--- a/jail/jail.c
+++ b/jail/jail.c
@@ -6369,7 +6369,7 @@ static void post_start_hook(void)
 	/* restore securebits back to normal (and lock them if not in userns) */
 	if (opts.capset.apply) {
 		if (prctl(PR_SET_SECUREBITS, jail_in_userns() ? 0 :
-		    SECBIT_KEEP_CAPS_LOCKED|SECBIT_NO_SETUID_FIXUP_LOCKED|SECBIT_NOROOT_LOCKED)) {
+		    SECBIT_NO_SETUID_FIXUP_LOCKED|SECBIT_NOROOT_LOCKED)) {
 			ERROR("prctl(PR_SET_SECUREBITS) failed: %m\n");
 			free_and_exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
 		}
